{"name":"Rave Regatta","hex":"#00619d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rave","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An enthusiastic review (such as of a play).","A large-scale dance party with strobe lights and fast-paced electronic dance music, often illegally organized open-air or in underground venues."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To be mentally unclear; to be delirious; to talk or act irrationally; to be wild, furious, or raging.","To speak or write wildly or incoherently."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rave"},{"term":"regatta","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A series of boat races, or sometimes a single race.","A striped cotton fabric."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/regatta"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rave","blocks":[{"text":"A rave is a dance party at a warehouse, club, or other public or private venue, typically featuring performances by DJs playing electronic dance music. The style is most associated with the early 1990s dance music scene when DJs played at illegal events in musical styles dominated by electronic dance music from a wide range of sub-genres, including acid house, techno, house, jungle, breakbeat, hardcore, happy hardcore, trance, trap and alternative dance. Occasionally live musicians have been known to perform at raves, in addition to other types of performance artists such as go-go dancers and fire dancers. The music is amplified with a large, powerful sound reinforcement system, typically with large subwoofers to produce a deep bass sound. The music is often accompanied by laser light shows, projected coloured images, visual effects and fog machines."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8d/Sven_Vath_playing_at_Amnesia.JPG/330px-Sven_Vath_playing_at_Amnesia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rave"},{"title":"Boat racing","blocks":[{"text":"Boat racing (Regatta) is a sport in which boats, or other types of watercraft, race on water. Boat racing powered by oars is recorded as having occurred in ancient Egypt, and it is likely that people have engaged in races involving boats and other water-borne craft for as long as such watercraft have existed."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boat_racing"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Mur_Ultim_Atom%26Biobanas.jpg/500px-Mur_Ultim_Atom%26Biobanas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Mur_Ultim_Atom%26Biobanas.jpg/500px-Mur_Ultim_Atom%26Biobanas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A huge bank of speakers and subwoofers from a rave sound reinforcement system","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMur_Ultim_Atom%26Biobanas.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Rave_-_Juiz_de_Fora_-_MG.jpg/500px-Rave_-_Juiz_de_Fora_-_MG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Rave_-_Juiz_de_Fora_-_MG.jpg/1280px-Rave_-_Juiz_de_Fora_-_MG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Rave_-_Juiz_de_Fora_-_MG.jpg/500px-Rave_-_Juiz_de_Fora_-_MG.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Rave – Juiz de Fora – MG, featuring bright psychedelic theming common at many raves","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARave_-_Juiz_de_Fora_-_MG.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Roland_TB-303_Panel.jpg/500px-Roland_TB-303_Panel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Roland_TB-303_Panel.jpg/1280px-Roland_TB-3